<section class="white-knowledge three-tool-knowledge" id="white-guide" aria-labelledby="white-guide-heading">
 <h2 id="white-guide-heading">White Days fasting calendar: 13, 14 and 15 Hijri explained</h2>
 <p><strong>Short answer:</strong> The White Days, or <strong>Ayyam al-Bid</strong>, are the <strong>13th, 14th and 15th days of each Islamic lunar month</strong>. Fasting them is a recommended voluntary practice outside months and dates with separate rules. Their Gregorian dates must be converted from the Hijri calendar and checked against local moon-sighting announcements.</p>
